using the given list of terms. Not all terms will be used."},{"type":"text","value":"Terms: analogue, binary, bit depth, byte, colour depth, digital, height, hertz, higher, lower, measuring, recording, repeated, sample rate, sampling, seconds, smaller, unique"},{"type":"text","value":"An ____ sound wave needs to be converted into a digital sound wave."},{"type":"text","value":"Sound ____ is when the amplitude of the sound wave is measured at set intervals."},{"type":"text","value":"The ____ is the number of times a second the sound wave is measured. This is given in Hertz."},{"type":"text","value":"Each amplitude is given a ____ binary number. The number of bits allocated to each sample is the ____."},{"type":"text","value":"The ____ the number of bits, the wider the number of amplitudes can be measured."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"1 mark for each correctly completed term to max 6."},{"type":"table","headers":["Gap","Answer"],"rows":[["Gap 1","analogue"],["Gap 2","sampling"],["Gap 3","sample rate"],["Gap 4","unique"],["Gap 5","bit depth"],["Gap 6","higher"]]},{"type":"text","value":"Do not accept 'smaller' for the final gap — the higher the number of bits, the wider the range of amplitudes that can be measured."}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Gap 1: analogue (an analogue sound wave needs to be converted into a digital sound wave)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Gap 2: sampling (sound sampling is when the amplitude of the sound wave is measured at set intervals)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Gap 3: sample rate (the number of times a second the sound wave is measured, given in Hertz)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Gap 4: unique (each amplitude is given a unique binary number)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Gap 5: bit depth (the number of bits allocated to each sample is the bit depth)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Gap 6: higher (the higher the number of bits, the wider the number of amplitudes that can be measured)","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27701_Computer_systems_June_2025 (1).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/question/page-002.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/markscheme/page-014.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/dev-qa/q-1-a.png"}},{"question_id":"1(b)(i)","parent_question":1,"topic":"pixel definition","marks":1,"command_word":"define","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The student creates 10 bitmap images using a computer."},{"type":"text","value":"Each image has a colour depth of 8-bits and a resolution of 800 x 500 pixels."},{"type":"text","value":"Define the term pixel."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"list","items":["1 mark from: the smallest unit/part of an image","or a (single) square/dot/diode which has one/single colour.","Accept 'block' or 'particle' in place of 'square' by benefit of the doubt.","Do not accept 'a square that contains many colours' — a pixel can only show one colour at any one time."]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"States that a pixel is the smallest unit/part of an image, OR a single square/dot with a single colour","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27701_Computer_systems_June_2025 (1).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/question/page-003.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/markscheme/page-014.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/dev-qa/q-1-b-i.png"}},{"question_id":"1(b)(ii)","parent_question":1,"topic":"image file size calculation","marks":2,"command_word":"calculate","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Calculate the total file size of the 10 images in kilobytes."},{"type":"text","value":"Show your working out."},{"type":"text","value":"Working: ____"},{"type":"text","value":"File size: ____ kilobytes"}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"1 mark for showing one stage of working, e.g.:"},{"type":"list","items":["800 * 500 = 400 000","or 400 000 * 10 = 4 000 000","or multiplying by 8 for bits then dividing by 8 for bytes","or dividing by 1000 to convert to kilobytes"]},{"type":"text","value":"Accept 8 * 5 for the resolution step by benefit of the doubt."},{"type":"text","value":"Accept any valid method: statements, grids, calculations."},{"type":"text","value":"1 mark for the final answer: 4000 kilobytes."},{"type":"text","value":"Accept division by 1024 instead of 1000, giving a final answer of 3906.25 kilobytes."},{"type":"text","value":"If no answer in the answer space, look for it clearly identified in the working."}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"At least one stage of valid working shown (e.g. 800 * 500, or 400 000 * 10, or converting bits to bytes to kilobytes)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Correct final answer: 4000 kilobytes (accept 3906.25 kilobytes if division by 1024 is used)","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27701_Computer_systems_June_2025 (1).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/question/page-003.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/markscheme/page-015.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/dev-qa/q-1-b-ii.png"}},{"question_id":"1(b)(iii)","parent_question":1,"topic":"colour depth bits","marks":1,"command_word":"state","content":[{"type":"text","value":"State the minimum number of bits that will be needed to represent 240 different colours."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for the answer 8. Allow any calculation that equates to 8 (e.g. 2^7 = 128 is not enough, 2^8 = 256 covers 240). Do not accept 2^8 or 256 as the final answer — the question asks for the number of bits.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Correct answer: 8 (bits)","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27701_Computer_systems_June_2025 (1).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/question/page-003.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/markscheme/p