inished","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27702_Computational_thinking_algorithms_and_programming_June_2023 (1).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-june/question/page-004.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-june/markscheme/page-023.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-june/dev-qa/q-1-d.png"}},{"question_id":"2(a)","parent_question":2,"topic":"syntax and logic errors","marks":2,"command_word":"state","content":[{"type":"text","value":"This pseudocode algorithm totals all the numbers in the 0-indexed array `scores`"},{"type":"code","language":"ocr-reference","value":"01 total = 0\\n02 for scoreCount = 1 to scores.length - 1\\n03   scores[scoreCount] = total + total\\n04 next scoreCount\\n05 print(total)"},{"type":"text","value":"The function `length` returns the number of elements in the array."},{"type":"text","value":"The algorithm contains several errors."},{"type":"text","value":"Two types of errors in a program are syntax and logic errors."},{"type":"text","value":"State what is meant by a syntax error and a logic error."},{"type":"text","value":"Syntax error: ____"},{"type":"text","value":"Logic error: ____"}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark each. The question asks for a definition; examples may strengthen the response but are not acceptable by themselves. Syntax error: an error in the rules/grammar of the programming language; program does not (fully) run / translate / execute / start. Logic error: produces incorrect / unexpected result/output; program runs / does not crash. Do not allow generic \\"error/problem in the code, does not work / does not do what designed/intended to do\\" for either. \\"Error in the syntax\\" or \\"error in the logic\\" are not enough even with examples.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Syntax error: breaks the rules/grammar of the language / prevents the program running or translating","marks":1},{"criteria":"Logic error: program runs