p (so the count is lost)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Error 2 line number: Line 07 (print(\\"empty\\"))","marks":1},{"criteria":"Error 2 explanation: prints out the string \\"empty\\" instead of the value held in the variable","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27702_Computational_thinking_algorithms_and_programming_Practice_2019 (1).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2019-practice/question/page-004.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2019-practice/markscheme/page-018.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-2-2019-practice/dev-qa/q-2-b-ii.png"}},{"question_id":"2(c)(i)","parent_question":2,"topic":"binary search steps","marks":4,"command_word":"show","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Each teacher has the assessment grades for each student. These grades are stored in numerical order."},{"type":"text","value":"The grades for one student are shown:"},{"type":"table","headers":[],"rows":[["2","3","4","5","6","7","8"]]},{"type":"text","value":"Show the steps that a binary search would take to check whether the student has achieved a grade 7 in any assessment."},{"type":"text","value":"Your answer must refer to the grades provided."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark per bullet to max 4. Answer must refer to the specific values in the list. Points: compare 5 (middle value) to 7; 5 is smaller than 7 / 7 is larger than 5, so discard the lower half of the list / repeat with the upper part of the list; compare 7 (new middle) to 7 — item found.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Compares the middle value (5) to the search value 7","marks":1},{"criteria":"Identifies that 5 is smaller than 7 (or 7 is larger than 5)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Discards the lower half of the list / repeats the process with the upper part of the list (6, 7, 8)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Compares 7 (new middle of the upper sub-list) to 7 — item found","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27702_Computational_th