ny seats are available in each screen. The name of the screen is passed in as a string parameter and the number of free seats is returned as an integer."},{"type":"text","value":"Write code using the function \`freeseats()\` to find the number of seats available in screen Red and assign this to a variable with identifier \`redseats\`."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for calling freeseats with \\"Red\\" as the argument; 1 mark for assigning the returned value to the variable redseats. Example: redseats = freeseats(\\"Red\\"). \\"Red\\" must use suitable string delimiters (e.g. speech marks) if the string is passed directly. Do not penalise case.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"freeseats called with \\"Red\\" as the argument (using appropriate string delimiters)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Returned value assigned to variable redseats (e.g. redseats = freeseats(\\"Red\\"))","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27702_Computational_thinking_algorithms_and_programming_Practice_2019 (1).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2019-practice/question/page-007.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2019-practice/markscheme/page-019.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-2-2019-practice/dev-qa/q-3-c.png"}},{"question_id":"4(a)","parent_question":4,"topic":"car dealership scenario","marks":0,"command_word":"context","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A car dealership uses a computer system to record details of the cars that it has for sale. Each car has a make, model, age and number of miles driven."},{"type":"text","value":"Each car is given a star rating of 1 to 5, based on the age of the car and the number of miles it has been driven. This rating is recorded in the computer system."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Context for parts (i), (ii) and (iii). No marks.","marks_breakdown":[]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27702_Computational_thinking_algorithms_and_programming_Practice_2019 (1).pdf","que