leage __________"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Answers: `DroneID, Mileage`; `FROM`; `AND`; `> 50000`. Accept `SELECT *` or selecting additional fields for the first marking point.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Selects DroneID and Mileage or equivalent valid fields","marks":1},{"criteria":"Uses FROM before TblDrone","marks":1},{"criteria":"Uses AND to add the mileage condition","marks":1},{"criteria":"Uses > 50000 for Mileage","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27702_Computational_thinking_algorithms_and_programming_Practice_2023 (2).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-practice/question/page-011.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-practice/markscheme/page-025.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-practice/dev-qa/q-7-a-i.png"}},{"question_id":"7(a)(ii)","parent_question":7,"topic":"flowchart algorithm completion","marks":2,"command_word":"complete","response_style":"annotate-image","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Drones must be checked every 10 000 miles. If the difference between `Mileage` and `LastCheck` is greater than 10 000 then the drone needs to be checked. The flowchart outputs `Check` if the drone needs to be checked and `No Check` if it does not need to be checked."},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the flowchart for the algorithm."},{"type":"image","kind":"diagram","src":"j277/yearpapers/paper2-2023-practice/7aii/flowchart.png","alt_text":"Flowchart with blank decision and output boxes for drone checking"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Decision should test `Mileage - LastCheck > 10000`. The output boxes should correctly show `Check` and `No Check` based on the logical check. If the comparison is reversed, allow follow-through for outputs that are consistently reversed.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Decision tests whether Mileage - LastCheck is greater than 10000","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputs Check and No Check correctly for the decision outcome","marks":1}]},"