ecute cycle."],["CU (Control Unit)",""],["","Stores the address of the data to be fetched from or the address where the data is to be stored."],["","Performs mathematical calculations and logical operations."]]}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for each missing term or definition. Row 1: Program Counter / PC. Row 2: the Control Unit synchronises, controls, or coordinates the processor, hardware, fetch-execute cycle, processes, or flow of data, or decodes instructions. Row 3: Memory Address Register / MAR. Row 4: Arithmetic Logic Unit / ALU.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Program Counter / PC identified",marks:1},{criteria:"Valid Control Unit definition",marks:1},{criteria:"Memory Address Register / MAR identified",marks:1},{criteria:"Arithmetic Logic Unit / ALU identified",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"4(a)(i)",parent_question:4,topic:"register and memory component identification",marks:4,command_word:"identify",content:[{type:"text",value:"The table has five components of a computer, and four statements."},{type:"text",value:"Tick one or more boxes in each row to identify which component(s) each statement describes."},{type:"table",headers:["Statement","MAR","MDR","Cache","Program Counter","RAM"],rows:[["It stores a single address","","","","",""],["It stores frequently used instructions","","","","",""],["It is a register","","","","",""],["It stores all currently running data and instructions","","","","",""]]}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for each row with correct ticks and blanks. Row 1: MAR and Program Counter. Row 2: Cache. Row 3: MAR, MDR, and Program Counter. Row 4: RAM. If extra ticks are added on a row, award 0 for that row.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Single-address row correct",marks:1},{criteria:"Frequently-used-instructions row correct",marks:1},{criteria:"Register row correct",marks:1},{criteria:"Currently running data and instructions row correct",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"4(a)(ii)",parent_question:4,topic:"register purposes",marks:3,command_word:"state",content:[{type:"text",value:"State the purpose of each of the following registers."},{type:"table",headers:["Register","Purpose"],rows:[["MAR",""],["MDR",""],["Program Counter",""]]}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark each for a correct purpose. MAR: holds the memory address of the instruction or data to be fetched from or written to memory. MDR: holds the data or instruction that has just been fetched from memory, or is about to be written to memory. Program Counter: stores the address of the next instruction to be fetched.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"MAR purpose correct",marks:1},{criteria:"MDR purpose correct",marks:1},{criteria:"Program Counter purpose correct",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"4(a)(iii)",parent_question:4,topic:"register purpose",marks:2,command_word:"identify and describe",content:[{type:"text",value:"Identify the name of a register other than the MAR, MDR, or Program Counter, and describe its purpose."},{type:"table",headers:["Register","Purpose"],rows:[["",""]]}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for a valid register other than MAR, MDR, or Program Counter, for example Accumulator (ACC) or Current Instruction Register (CIR). 1 mark for a matching description, for example the Accumulator stores the result of arithmetic or logical operations, or the CIR stores the instruction currently being executed.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Valid register other than MAR, MDR, or Program Counter identified",marks:1},{criteria:"Matching register purpose described",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"4(b)",parent_question:4,topic:"clock speed and processor performance",marks:2,command_word:"explain",content:[{type:"text",value:"Computer A has a single core, 3.2 GHz processor."},{type:"text",value:"Computer B has a single core, 1.2 GHz processor."},{type:"text",value:"Explain why Computer A will usually run faster than Computer B."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark per point. Computer A has a faster / higher clock speed. At 3.2 GHz it can run more fetch-execute cycles per second, so more instructions can be executed per second.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Higher clock speed identified",marks:1},{criteria:"More cycles / instructions per second explained",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"5",parent_question:5,topic:"fetch-execute cycle events",marks:2,command_word:"identify",content:[{type:"text",value:"Identify two events that take place during the fetch-execute cycle."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for each correct event to max 2. Acceptable events include: an instruction is fetched from memory; the instruction is decoded; the instruction is executed; the process is repeated; the program counter is incremented; the instruction is transferred to the MDR; the address of the instruction to be fetched is placed in the MAR.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"First correct fetch-execute cycle event",marks:1},{criteria:"Second correct fetch-execute cycle event",marks:1}]}}],y5={paper_id:d5,qualification:u5,component:p5,title:h5,year:m5,session:f5,total_marks:g5,questions:_5},w5="J277-TOPIC-1.1.2",b5="J277",k5="TOPIC",v5="CPU Performance",x5=null,C5=null,q5=8,S5=[{question_id:"1",parent_question:1,topic:"CPU performance characteristics",marks:3,command_word:"give",content:[{type:"text",value:"A computer has a Central Processing Unit (CPU)."},{type:"text",value:"Give three characteristics of a CPU that can affect its performance."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark each to max 3. Clock speed, cache size, and number of cores. 'clock', 'cache', 'speed', or 'cores' on their own are not enough.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Clock speed",marks:1},{criteria:"Cache size",marks:1},{criteria:"Number of cores",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2(a)",parent_question:2,topic:"number of cores and performance",marks:1,command_word:"identify",content:[{type:"text",value:"The specification of two CPUs is shown in Fig. 1."},{type:"table",headers:["Computer 1","Computer 2"],rows:[["Clock Speed: 1 GHz","Clock Speed: 1.4 GHz"],["Cache size: 2 MB","Cache size: 2 MB"],["Number of Cores: 4","Number of Cores: 2"]]},{type:"text",value:"When running a 3D flight simulator, Computer 1 is likely to run faster than Computer 2."},{type:"text",value:"Using the information in Fig. 1, identify one reason for this."}],answer:{guidance:"Correct answer: it has more cores. Accept equivalent answers explaining that Computer 1 can split work across more cores.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"More cores identified as the reason",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2(b)",parent_question:2,topic:"other components affecting performance",marks:2,command_word:"identify",content:[{type:"text",value:"The specification of two CPUs is shown in Fig. 1."},{type:"table",headers:["Computer 1","Computer 2"],rows:[["Clock Speed: 1 GHz","Clock Speed: 1.4 GHz"],["Cache size: 2 MB","Cache size: 2 MB"],["Number of Cores: 4","Number of Cores: 2"]]},{type:"text",value:"Identify two other parts of a computer that are not in Fig. 1, which could improve the performance of the computers."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark each. Accept RAM, SSD, HDD, or graphics card (GPU). Other appropriate responses such as motherboard or sound card may also be accepted.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"First valid computer component identified",marks:1},{criteria:"Second valid computer component identified",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2(c)",parent_question:2,topic:"cache size and performance",marks:2,command_word:"explain",content:[{type:"text",value:"Explain one reason why the cache size affects the performance of the CPU."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for a correct point and 1 mark for the linked explanation. For example: data is transferred faster, which makes the CPU more efficient; or it is faster to transfer data to and from cache than to and from RAM.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Valid point about faster cache access",marks:1},{criteria:"Linked explanation of improved efficiency or comparison with RAM",marks:1}]}}],A5={paper_id:w5,qualification:b5,component:k5,title:v5,year:x5,session:C5,total_marks:q5,questions:S5},j5="J277-TOPIC-1.1.3",O5="J277",T5="TOPIC",P5="Embedded Systems",J5=null,I5=null,E5=10,R5=[{question_id:"1",parent_question:1,topic:"embedded system characteristics",marks:3,command_word:"explain",content:[{type:"text",value:"A car has a 'Follow Me' system that uses a cruise control feature to allow the car to follow the car in front of it."},{type:"text",value:"It will keep the same speed and distance without the driver's intervention. The cruise control system is an example of an embedded system."},{type:"text",value:"Explain the reasons why the 'Follow Me' system is an example of an embedded system."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark each to max 3. Valid points include: it has a specific purpose / only performs one limited task; it is built within a larger device or car; it has dedicated hardware or sensors; it has a microprocessor; it uses built-in software / firmware / ROM; its operation is hard to change or update; it is an automated control system.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"One valid reason linked to embedded-system characteristics",marks:1},{criteria:"Second valid reason",marks:1},{criteria:"Third valid reason",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2",parent_question:2,topic:"embedded systems in cars",marks:3,command_word:"identify and explain",content:[{type:"text",value:"A car comes with many embedded systems, for example parking sensors."},{type:"text",value:"Identify one other embedded system that could be found in a car and explain why this is an embedded system."},{type:"table",headers:["Example embedded system","Explanation"],rows:[["",""]]}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for a suitable example such as auto lights, auto window wipers, sat nav / GPS, air conditioning / climate control, radio / infotainment, lane assist, engine management system, auto-park, cruise control, auto-brake, Follow-me, or dashcam. 1 mark each to max 2 for explanation, e.g. limited functions, dedicated microprocessor, or hard to change function. Do not award simply 'built into the car / larger machine' because that is already given in the question.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Valid embedded-system example in a car",marks:1},{criteria:"First valid explanation point",marks:1},{criteria:"Second valid explanation point",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"3",parent_question:3,topic:"embedded systems terminology",marks:4,command_word:"complete",content:[{type:"text",value:"The following paragraph describes embedded systems."},{type:"text",value:"Complete the paragraph by selecting terms from the list and writing them in the correct places. Not all terms are used."},{type:"text",value:"Terms: actuator, applications, change, functions, laptop, larger, lights, microprocessor, processor, range, smaller, washing machine"},{type:"text",value:"Embedded systems have limited _____. They are often built into a _____ machine. Two examples of embedded systems are a _____ and automated _____ in a car."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for each completed term. functions; larger; washing machine; lights.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"functions",marks:1},{criteria:"larger",marks:1},{criteria:"washing machine",marks:1},{criteria:"lights",marks:1}]}}],D5={paper_id:j5,qualification:O5,component:T5,title:P5,year:J5,session:I5,total_marks:E5,questions:R5},M5="J277-TOPIC-1.2.10",N5="J277",L5="TOPIC",B5="Data storage: Numbers",F5=null,$5=null,z5=10,W5=[{question_id:"1(a)",parent_question:1,topic:"terabytes to megabytes conversion",marks:1,command_word:"identify",content:[{type:"text",value:"Tick one box to identify the quantity of megabytes that is the same as 2 terabytes."},{type:"table",headers:["","2000 MB","20 000 MB","200 000 MB","2 000 000 MB"],rows:[["Select","","","",""]]}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark. Correct answer: 2 000 000 MB.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Correct answer: 2 000 000 MB",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"1(b)",parent_question:1,topic:"denary, binary, and hexadecimal conversion table",marks:4,command_word:"complete",content:[{type:"text",value:"Each row in the table contains a number that is written as a denary value, 8-bit binary value, and a 2-digit hexadecimal value. Some values are missing."},{type:"text",value:"Complete the table by writing in the missing value for each number."},{type:"table",headers:["Denary","8-bit binary","2-digit hexadecimal"],rows:[["38","","26"],["","01001110","4E"],["156","10011100",""],["215","","D7"]]}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for each completed row. The missing values are 00100110, 78, 9C, and 11010111.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"38 = 00100110 = 26",marks:1},{criteria:"78 = 01001110 = 4E",marks:1},{criteria:"156 = 10011100 = 9C",marks:1},{criteria:"215 = 11010111 = D7",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"1(c)",parent_question:1,topic:"binary addition",marks:2,command_word:"complete",content:[{type:"text",value:"Complete the binary addition of these two 8-bit binary numbers: 01110011 + 00110100. Show your working out."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for correct working with the carries shown and 1 mark for the correct answer 10100111.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Correct binary working is shown with the required carries",marks:1},{criteria:"Correct answer: 10100111",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"1(d)",parent_question:1,topic:"right binary shift result",marks:1,command_word:"identify",content:[{type:"text",value:"Tick one box to identify the result of a 2-place right binary shift on the binary number 01110111."},{type:"table",headers:["","00011101","11101110","00111011","11011100"],rows:[["Select","","","",""]]}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark. Correct answer: 00011101.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Correct answer: 00011101",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"1(e)",parent_question:1,topic:"binary shift to multiply by 8",marks:2,command_word:"describe",content:[{type:"text",value:"Describe the binary shift that can be used to multiply any number by 8."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for identifying a left shift and 1 mark for identifying that the shift is 3 places.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Left shift",marks:1},{criteria:"3 places",marks:1}]}}],Q5={paper_id:M5,qualification:N5,component:L5,title:B5,year:F5,session:$5,total_marks:z5,questions:W5},V5="J277-TOPIC-1.2.1",U5="J277",H5="TOPIC",G5="Primary storage (Memory)",X5=null,Y5=null,K5=14,Z5=[{question_id:"1(i)",parent_question:1,topic:"need for primary and secondary storage",marks:2,command_word:"explain",content:[{type:"text",value:"An artist has a computer that they use to create images."},{type:"text",value:"Their computer has both hardware and software."},{type:"text",value:"The hardware includes primary and secondary storage."},{type:"text",value:"Explain why a computer needs both primary and secondary storage."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark each. Primary storage is needed for the active data, instructions, software, or operating system that the processor needs to access. Secondary storage is needed to store files and data long-term or permanently when the power is off.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Primary storage is needed for active data, instructions, software, or start-up access",marks:1},{criteria:"Secondary storage is needed for long-term or permanent storage when the computer is turned off",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"1(ii)",parent_question:1,topic:"secondary storage device and stored data",marks:2,command_word:"give",content:[{type:"text",value:"An artist has a computer that they use to create images."},{type:"text",value:"Give one example of a secondary storage device that the artist's computer will have and an example of the data that will be stored on it."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for a valid secondary storage device and 1 mark for a valid example of data stored on it. Devices could include a hard drive, SSD, USB memory stick, flash memory card, CD, or DVD. Example data could include created images, documents, software, files, or data moved from RAM to virtual memory.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"A valid secondary storage device is identified",marks:1},{criteria:"A valid example of data stored on that device is given",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"1(iii)",parent_question:1,topic:"virtual memory statements",marks:4,command_word:"complete",content:[{type:"text",value:"The computer has Virtual Memory (VM)."},{type:"text",value:"The table has four statements about VM. Not all of the statements are correct."},{type:"text",value:"Tick the True column for the statements that are correct. Rewrite any statement that is incorrect in the False column by changing the statement to make it true."},{type:"table",headers:["Statement","True","False - rewrite the statement to make it true"],rows:[["A section of primary storage is partitioned to act as virtual memory","",""],["Data from ROM is transferred into VM","",""],["VM is needed when RAM is full, or nearly full","",""],["Data from VM is transferred back to secondary storage when needed","",""]]}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for each row. Row 1 should be corrected to secondary storage. Row 2 should be corrected to RAM. Row 3 is true. Row 4 should be corrected so data from VM is transferred back to RAM when needed.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Row 1 corrected to secondary storage",marks:1},{criteria:"Row 2 corrected to RAM",marks:1},{criteria:"Row 3 identified as true",marks:1},{criteria:"Row 4 corrected so data is transferred back to RAM",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2(i)",parent_question:2,topic:"RAM and ROM difference",marks:1,command_word:"state",content:[{type:"text",value:"A smart television allows the user to search the Internet and watch videos online."},{type:"text",value:"A smart television has both RAM and ROM."},{type:"text",value:"State the difference between RAM and ROM."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark. ROM is non-volatile while RAM is volatile, or ROM usually cannot be changed while RAM can be changed. A valid answer must state both sides of the difference.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"A valid two-sided difference between RAM and ROM is stated",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2(ii)",parent_question:2,topic:"RAM data examples",marks:2,command_word:"give",content:[{type:"text",value:"Give two examples of data that a smart television could store in RAM."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark each to a maximum of 2. Valid examples include a running web browser or application, parts of the operating system currently running, the current video or programme being watched, buffered data, button presses from the user, current volume, current channel, or the current source such as HDMI1.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"One valid example of data currently stored in RAM",marks:1},{criteria:"A second valid example of data currently stored in RAM",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"3",parent_question:3,topic:"RAM and ROM in a sat nav",marks:3,command_word:"identify",content:[{type:"text",value:"A satellite navigation system (Sat Nav) uses RAM and ROM."},{type:"text",value:"Tick one box in each row to show whether each of the statements is true for the RAM or ROM in a Sat Nav."},{type:"table",headers:["Statement","RAM","ROM"],rows:[["Stores the boot up sequence of the Sat Nav.","",""],["The contents are lost when the Sat Nav is turned off.","",""],["Holds copies of open maps and routes.","",""]]}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for each correct row. The boot up sequence is ROM. Contents lost when the Sat Nav is turned off is RAM. Open maps and routes are RAM.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Boot up sequence identified as ROM",marks:1},{criteria:"Contents lost when turned off identified as RAM",marks:1},{criteria:"Open maps and routes identified as RAM",marks:1}]}}],e4={paper_id:V5,qualification:U5,component:H5,title:G5,year:X5,session:Y5,total_marks:K5,questions:Z5},t4="J277-TOPIC-1.2.2",a4="J277",r4="TOPIC",n4="Secondary storage",i4=null,s4=null,o4=34,c4=JSON.parse(`[{"question_id":"1","parent_question":1,"topic":"choosing portable secondary storage","marks":4,"command_word":"identify and justify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A student is creating a presentation containing images and sound."},{"type":"text","value":"The student wants to use a secondary storage device to move their files to their home computer."},{"type":"text","va