omputer system is created to sell tickets and store information about visitors and the music acts."},{"type":"text","value":"The database table TblMusic stores data about the music acts. Some of the data in TblMusic is shown:"},{"type":"table","headers":["ActID","Stage","Day","SetLength"],"rows":[["1","Platinum","Saturday","0.5"],["2","Hills","Saturday","1.5"],["3","Triangle","Sunday","1.0"],["4","Platinum","Sunday","0.5"]]},{"type":"text","value":"An SQL statement has been written to show ActID and Stage for all acts playing on Saturday. The SQL statement is incorrect."},{"type":"code","language":"sql","value":"SELECT ActID AND Stage\\nFROM TblActs\\nIF Day = Saturday"},{"type":"text","value":"Refine the SQL statement to correct the errors."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"One mark per refinement. Correct SQL:"},{"type":"code","language":"sql","value":"SELECT ActID, Stage\\nFROM TblMusic\\nWHERE Day = \\"Saturday\\""},{"type":"list","items":["Allow descriptions of change.","Allow quote marks around field and table names.","Allow == for BP4.","Spellings/spaces in field/table names must be accurate.","Ignore case.","Max 3 if final SQL is invalid/in wrong order/has extra superfluous code."]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Replace AND with a comma between ActID and Stage (SELECT ActID, Stage)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Correct table name to TblMusic (FROM TblMusic)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Replace IF with WHERE","marks":1},{"criteria":"Add quotation marks around Saturday (Day = \\"Saturday\\")","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(a)(ii)","parent_question":1,"topic":"records (database records)","marks":1,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Identify one example of a record from TblMusic."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Any example of one complete record/row from the table given, or any example of one complete record/row that could potentially be added to the table. Accept any sensible data for new record as long as 4 distinct items of data given. Allow field names with data. Ignore order of data. Ignore case/spelling. Ignore data types. Do not allow definition of a record.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Complete record/row with four distinct field values, e.g. 1, Platinum, Saturday, 0.5","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(a)(iii)","parent_question":1,"topic":"data types for fields","marks":2,"command_word":"give","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Give the most appropriate data type for each field shown."},{"type":"table","headers":["Field name","Data stored","Data type"],"rows":[["Stage","The name of the stage",""],["SetLength","The length of each set in hours",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"Accept equivalent data types, including those common in databases: String = text/varchar/char etc; Real/Float = decimal/single/double/numeric etc.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Stage: String (or equivalent e.g. text/varchar/char)","marks":1},{"criteria":"SetLength: Real / Float (or equivalent e.g. decimal/single/double/numeric)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(b)(i)","parent_question":1,"topic":"sub-programs (functions, parameters, return)","marks":4,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Tickets to the festival are £60 each. Visitors can buy multiple tickets. For example, a visitor buying 4 tickets would pay £240."},{"type":"text","value":"Write a function, calculatePrice() that:\\n• takes the number of tickets to be purchased as a parameter\\n• calculates and returns the total price to pay.\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• a high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Section B so must be high level code. Example code:\\nfunction calculatePrice(num)\\n    price = num * 60\\n    return price\\nendfunction\\nAll code must be within function definition (if present). BP3 - if no parameter present, allow multiplying by sensible value. FT overwriting parameter. BP4 must be return; do not credit output/print. Accept multiple parameters passed in. Accept returning by assigning to function name (e.g. VB).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Function definition for calculatePrice()","marks":1},{"criteria":"...with parameter that is not overwritten","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculate price based on multiplying parameter (if present) by 60","marks":1},{"criteria":"...always return calculated price","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(b)(ii)","parent_question":1,"topic":"sub-programs (calling a function)","marks":2,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Write an algorithm that:\\n• uses the function calculatePrice() to find the price for a visitor buying 3 tickets\\n• stores the result in the variable totalPrice\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• a high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example code: totalPrice = calculatePrice(3). Do not accept == for assignment. Allow FT to BP2 only if sensible attempt at BP1. Allow multiple values passed in as long as 3 is one of the values. Do not accept definitions of a function - must be calling the existing function.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"calculatePrice(3) called (with 3 as parameter)","marks":1},{"criteria":"...return value assigned to totalPrice","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(c)(i)","parent_question":1,"topic":"arrays (1D) and trace tables","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The number of different music acts on each of the three stages is stored in the array `actNumbers`. Each index of the array represents one stage."},{"type":"table","headers":["Index","0","1","2"],"rows":[["Data","10","14","6"]],"caption":"actNumbers"},{"type":"text","value":"This algorithm adds up the total number of acts on all three stages."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"01 count = 0\\n02 for x = 0 to 2\\n03   count = count + actNumbers[x]\\n04 next x\\n05 print(count)"},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the trace table for the algorithm. You may not need to use all rows in the table."},{"type":"table","headers":["Line number","count","x","Output"],"rows":[["","","",""],["","","",""],["","","",""],["","","",""],["","","",""],["","","",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"Based on example data where actNumbers = [10, 14, 6]. Ignore line numbers - not required. Mark order of values. Values can be repeated in count and x columns, look at changes. FT for BP4 if incorrect answer calculated but output.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"count initially set to 0","marks":1},{"criteria":"count increases to 10, 24, 30 and no other changes","marks":1},{"criteria":"x goes from 0, 1, 2 (, 3) and no other changes","marks":1},{"criteria":"30 output and no other output","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(c)(ii)","parent_question":1,"topic":"arrays (1D) - modifying a loop bound","marks":2,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The array `actNumbers` is changed to include data for two more stages. The new array is shown."},{"type":"table","headers":["Index","0","1","2","3","4"],"rows":[["Data","10","14","6","9","11"]],"caption":"actNumbers"},{"type":"text","value":"The algorithm from part (i) needs refining to work for the new array. The algorithm is repeated here:"},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"01 count = 0\\n02 for x = 0 to 2\\n03   count = count + actNumbers[x]\\n04 next x\\n05 print(count)"},{"type":"text","value":"Identify the line number that will need to be changed for the new array and write the updated line of code.\\n\\nLine number ____\\nUpdated code ____"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Must use x as counter variable. Accept rewrites in other languages. BOD 0 to 5 / range(5) etc. Accept other changes that implement the change successfully, e.g. using length of actNumbers.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Line 02 identified","marks":1},{"criteria":"For x = 0 to 4 (or equivalent, e.g. for x = 0 to len(actNumbers)-1)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(c)(iii)","parent_question":1,"topic":"string manipulation (output concatenation)","marks":1,"command_word":"refine","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Refine line 05 in the algorithm to output `\\"The total act count is \\"` and then the content of the variable `count`"},{"type":"text","value":"For example:"},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"The total act count is 50"},{"type":"text","value":"New line 05 ____"}],"answer":{"guidance":"print(\\"The total act count is \\" + count). Allow other concatenation operators e.g. & (VB), dot (PHP, Rust), double dot (Lua) etc. Allow comma. Must have some form of separator. Ignore spacing, case, casting. Allow other commands equivalent to print (e.g. echo, output). Allow string interpolation e.g. f strings in Python, $count in PHP.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"print(\\"The total act count is \\" + count) or equivalent with suitable separator and variable outside quotes","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(a)(i)","parent_question":2,"topic":"data types","marks":3,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Students take part in a sports day. The students are put into teams. Students gain points depending on their result and the year group they are in. The points are added to the team score. The team with the most points at the end of the sports day wins. Data about the teams and students is stored in a sports day program."},{"type":"text","value":"Identify the most appropriate data type for each variable used by the program. Each data type must be different."},{"type":"table","headers":["Variable","Example","Data type"],"rows":[["teamName","\\"Super-Team\\"",""],["studentYearGroup","11",""],["javelinThrow","18.2",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"Accept alternative equivalent correct data types (e.g. single/double/decimal for BP3). Do not accept char for BP1. Each data type must be different.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"teamName: String","marks":1},{"criteria":"studentYearGroup: Integer","marks":1},{"criteria":"javelinThrow: Real / Float","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(a)(ii)","parent_question":2,"topic":"arrays (1D) and sub-programs (linear search function)","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The student names for a team are stored in an array with the identifier `theTeam`. An example of the data in this array is shown."},{"type":"table","headers":["Index","0","1","2","3","4","5"],"rows":[["Data","Ali","Eve","Ling","Nina","Sarah","Tom"]],"caption":"theTeam"},{"type":"text","value":"A linear search function is used to find whether a student is in the team. The function:\\n• takes a student name as a parameter\\n• returns `True` if the student name is in the array\\n• returns `False` if the student name is **not** in the array."},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the design of an algorithm for the linear search function."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"function linearSearch(studentName)\\n  for count = 0 to ____\\n    if theTeam[____] == ____ then\\n      return ____\\n    endif\\n  next count\\n  return False\\nendfunction"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Accept 6 // theTeam.length() for BP1 (Python). Accept alternative length functions e.g. len(). Accept count = 5 for BP1. Accept \\"True\\" for BP4. Do not allow obvious spaces in variable names. Ignore capitalisation.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Upper bound: theTeam.length() - 1 // 5 (or equivalent)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Array index: count","marks":1},{"criteria":"Comparison value: studentName","marks":1},{"criteria":"Return value: True","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(b)","parent_question":2,"topic":"trace tables (selection, conditions)","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"This algorithm calculates the number of points a student gets for the distance they throw in the javelin:"},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"01 javelinThrow = input(\\"Enter distance\\")\\n02 yearGroup = input(\\"Enter year group\\")\\n03 if javelinThrow >= 20.0 then\\n04   score = 3\\n05 elseif javelinThrow >= 10.0 then\\n06   score = 2\\n07 else\\n08   score = 1\\n09 endif\\n10 if yearGroup != 11 then\\n11   score = score * 2\\n12 endif\\n13 print(\\"The score is\\", score)"},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the trace table for the algorithm when a student in year 10 throws a distance of 14.3. You may not need to use all the rows in the table."},{"type":"table","headers":["Line number","javelinThrow","yearGroup","score","Output"],"rows":[["","","","",""],["","","","",""],["","","","",""],["","","","",""],["","","","",""],["","","","",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"Max 3 if in wrong order or additional (incorrect) changes. Penalise line numbers once then FT. Allow FT for BP4 for current value of score. BP4 must not include comma. Ignore superfluous spaces/quotation marks.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"javelinThrow set to 14.3 on line 01 and yearGroup set to 10 on line 02","marks":1},{"criteria":"score set to 2 on line 06","marks":1},{"criteria":"score set to 4 on line 11","marks":1},{"criteria":"\\"The score is 4\\" output on line 13 with no additional outputs","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(c)(i)","parent_question":2,"topic":"input validation (selection)","marks":4,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The height a student jumps in the high jump needs to be input and validated. The height is entered in centimetres (cm) and must be between 40.0 and 180.0 inclusive."},{"type":"text","value":"Write an algorithm to:\\n• take the height jumped as input\\n• output \\"VALID\\" or \\"NOT VALID\\" depending on the height input.\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example 1:\\nh = input(\\"Enter height jumped\\")\\nif h >= 40 and h <= 180 then\\n  print(\\"valid\\")\\nelse\\n  print(\\"not valid\\")\\nendif\\nAnswers using AND/OR for BP2 and BP3 must be logically correct. BP4 needs reasonable attempt at either BP2 or BP3. Allow FT for BP4.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Inputs a value from the user and stores/uses it","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks min value (>= 40.0 // < 40)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks max value (<=180.0 // > 180)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputs both valid / not valid correctly based on checks","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(c)(ii)","parent_question":2,"topic":"test data (normal, boundary, erroneous)","marks":3,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The algorithm is tested using a range of tests. Complete the table to identify an example of test data for each type of test."},{"type":"table","headers":["Test data (height jumped in cm)","Type of test","Expected output"],"rows":[["","Normal","\\"VALID\\""],["","Boundary","\\"VALID\\""],["","Erroneous","\\"NOT VALID\\""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"No need to include decimals, e.g. accept 50. Ignore cm if given. Answer must be actual data (e.g. 50) and not description of data.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Normal: any value between 40 and 180 inclusive (e.g. 50)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Boundary: 40.0 // 180.0","marks":1},{"criteria":"Erroneous: any value less than 40 // greater than 180 // non-numeric value","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(d)","parent_question":2,"topic":"SQL SELECT/FROM/WHERE","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The individual results for each student in each event are stored in a database. The database table TblResult stores the times of students in the 100 m race. Some of the data is shown:"},{"type":"table","headers":["StudentID","YearGroup","TeamName","Time"],"rows":[["11GC1","11","Valiants",""],["10VE1","10","Super-Team","20.3"],["10SM1","10","Super-Team","19.7"],["11JP2","11","Champions","19.2"],["","","","19.65"]]},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the SQL statement to show the Student ID and team name of all students who are in year group 11."},{"type":"code","language":"sql","value":"SELECT StudentID, ____\\nFROM ____\\n____"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Max 3 if not in correct order / includes other logical errors. Ignore capitals. Do not accept * or additional fields for BP1. Spelling must be accurate (e.g. not TblResults). Accept == for BP4.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"TeamName in first space","marks":1},{"criteria":"TblResult in second space","marks":1},{"criteria":"WHERE","marks":1},{"criteria":"YearGroup = 11","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(e)(i)","parent_question":2,"topic":"abstraction (in program design)","marks":1,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Abstraction and decomposition have been used in the design of the sports day program."},{"type":"text","value":"Identify one way that abstraction has been used in the design of this program."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Must be applicable to this program (in the context of students and a sports day), not a generic description of what abstraction is. Examples: \'focus on student names and events\'; \'ignore data such as students\' favourite subjects\'; \'store year groups instead of ages or DOB\'; \'shows student IDs instead of full student details\'.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Any example of simplification / removing data or focussing on data in the design (applied to the sports day context)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(e)(ii)","parent_question":2,"topic":"decomposition (in program design)","marks":1,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Identify one way that decomposition has been used in the design of this program."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Must be applicable to this program, not a generic description. Examples: \'splits the program up into different events\'; \'separates the validation routines into subroutines\'; \'breaks the database down into a table per event\'. Do not give answers discussing splitting into fields only.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Any example of breaking down the program into sections/subroutines, or breaking down the database into tables (applied to the sports day context)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(f)","parent_question":2,"topic":"iteration with input, highest value algorithm","marks":6,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"An algorithm works out which team has won (has the highest score)."},{"type":"text","value":"Write an algorithm to:\\n• prompt the user to enter a team name and score, or to enter \\"stop\\" to stop entering new teams\\n• repeatedly take team names and scores as input until the user enters \\"stop\\"\\n• calculate which team has the highest score\\n• output the team name and score of the winning team in an appropriate message.\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied"}],"guidance_note":"","answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nhighscore = 0\\nwhile team != \\"stop\\"\\n   team = input(\\"enter team name\\")\\n   score = input(\\"enter score\\")\\n   if score > highscore then\\n     highscore = score\\n     highteam = team\\n   endif\\nendwhile\\nprint(highscore)\\nprint(highteam)\\nAllow use of break to exit loop. Allow use of recursive function(s) for BP2/3. Assume variables are 0/empty if not initialised. Allow arrays/lists or max/sum functions. FT for BP6.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Input team name AND score and store/use separately","marks":1},{"criteria":"Attempt at using iteration","marks":1},{"criteria":"...to enter team/score until \\"stop\\" entered","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates highest score","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates winning team name","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputs highest score and team name","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"3(a)","parent_question":3,"topic":"string manipulation (length, upper, left, right, casting)","marks":3,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The variable `message` is assigned a value."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"message = \\"abcd1234\\""},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the table to show the output when each statement executes. The first output has been completed for you."},{"type":"table","headers":["Statement","Output"],"rows":[["print(message.length)","8"],["print(message.upper)",""],["print(message.left(4))",""],["print(int(message.right(4))*2)",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"Case must be correct but BOD if ambiguous. Allow quotation marks in answer. 1 mark for each output.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"print(message.upper) -> ABCD1234 (upper case)","marks":1},{"criteria":"print(message.left(4)) -> abcd (lower case)","marks":1},{"criteria":"print(int(message.right(4))*2) -> 2468","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"3(b)","parent_question":3,"topic":"string manipulation (concatenation)","marks":3,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Write an algorithm in pseudocode to:\\n• store \\"Hello\\" in the variable word1\\n• store \\"Everyone\\" in the variable word2\\n• concatenate word1 and word2 to store \\"HelloEveryone\\" in the variable message"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nword1 = \\"Hello\\"\\nword2 = \\"Everyone\\"\\nmessage = word1 + word2\\nAccept & / + / . etc as valid methods of concatenation. Allow use of sensible concatenation functions e.g. concat(). Do not allow commas. Do not allow == for assigning value. Do not allow spaces in variable names. Reasonable attempt at BP2 needed to access BP3.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Storing both strings correctly in word1 and word2","marks":1},{"criteria":"Correct concatenation (word1 then word2)","marks":1},{"criteria":"...storing in variable message","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"4(a)","parent_question":4,"topic":"file handling (open/write/close)","marks":4,"command_word":"design","content":[{"type":"text","value":"OCR Drones flies goods around the country using drones. A text file is used to store pilot\'s codes and date of birth. The text file is named `pilots.txt`. The contents of some of this file is shown:"},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"JP670,17/05/1986\\nCC200,31/06/1980\\nSM720,01/04/1976\\nGC730,06/06/1978"},{"type":"text","value":"Design an algorithm to:\\n• Ask the user to input a pilot code and a date of birth\\n• Write these inputs to the `pilots.txt` text file"}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"One mark per bullet point. Award BP4 for implicit closing of file (e.g. using `with...` in Python). Allow data to be written either by writing both values or by concatenating into one string with a separating comma."},{"type":"text","value":"Example answer:"},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"dronepilotData = open(\\"pilots.txt\\")\\npilotCode = input(\\"enter code\\")\\ndob = input(\\"enter date of birth\\")\\ndronepilotData.writeLine(pilotCode, dob)\\ndronepilotData.close()"}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Ask the user for two inputs and store/use these","marks":1},{"criteria":"Open pilots.txt (for write/append)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Write both inputs to opened text file","marks":1},{"criteria":"Close text file (implicit closing acceptable)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"4(b)","parent_question":4,"topic":"2D arrays and sub-programs (function with casting)","marks":6,"command_word":"create","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A pilot is allowed to fly a maximum of 9 hours per day. The pilot code and the hours flown for each flight in one day are stored in a 2D array of strings with the identifier `journeys`. The data in `journeys` is shown."},{"type":"table","headers":["Index","Column [0]","Column [1]"],"rows":[["[0]","\\"SM720\\"","\\"4.5\\""],["[1]","\\"GC730\\"","\\"3\\""],["[2]","\\"JP670\\"","\\"2\\""],["[3]","\\"GC730\\"","\\"3.5\\""],["[4]","\\"CC200\\"","\\"9\\""],["[5]","\\"RY320\\"","\\"12\\""]],"caption":"journeys"},{"type":"text","value":"The value of `journeys[3,1]` is `\\"3.5\\"`."},{"type":"text","value":"Create a function, pilotValid(), that:\\n• takes a pilot code as a parameter\\n• uses the 2D array journeys to calculate the number of hours that the pilot has flown\\n• returns valid if the pilot has flown 9 hours or fewer or warning if the pilot has flown for more than 9 hours\\n• uses casting where needed.\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nfunction pilotValid(pilotCode)\\n  total = 0\\n  status = \\"\\"\\n  for i = 0 to 5\\n    if journeys[i,0] == pilotCode then\\n      temp = float(journeys[i,1])\\n      total = total + temp\\n    endif\\n  next i\\n  if total > 9 then\\n    status = \\"warning\\"\\n  else\\n    status = \\"valid\\"\\n  endif\\n  return status\\nendfunction\\nDo not allow casting to integer for BP4; data shows decimal places. Allow FT for BP5 and BP7. Max 6 marks.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Function header pilotValid() with (at least one) parameter","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks array element [i,0] for each item, calculates total","marks":1},{"criteria":"Casting to float / real","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks if 9 hours or fewer","marks":1},{"criteria":"Returns a value","marks":1},{"criteria":"...returns \\"warning\\" and \\"valid\\" correctly","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"5(i)","parent_question":5,"topic":"iteration, selection, string length","marks":6,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A player enters a code at the beginning of a computer game. The code is three characters long. The code sets the level of the game. The game has three levels. A variable level is assigned a value based on the code entered."},{"type":"text","value":"Write an algorithm that:\\n• asks the user to enter a three-character code\\n• repeats the previous step if the code is not 3 characters long\\n• if the code entered is SVA, assigns the value 2 to level\\n• if the code entered is UTV, assigns the value 3 to level\\n• assigns the value 1 to level if any other three-character code is entered."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nlevel = 0\\ncode = \\"\\"\\nwhile code.length != 3 then\\n  code = input(\\"enter a 3 character code\\")\\nendwhile\\nswitch code :\\n  case \\"SVA\\":\\n    level = 2\\n  case \\"UTV\\":\\n    level = 3\\n  default:\\n    level = 1\\nendswitch\\nAlternative with if/elseif/else also accepted.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Input code from user and store/use","marks":1},{"criteria":"Repeat for non-three character codes","marks":1},{"criteria":"Check for one code (SVA)","marks":1},{"criteria":"...and set level appropriately (level = 2 for SVA)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Check for and set level for 2nd code (UTV -> level = 3)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Set level to 1 for any other 3 character code","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"5(ii)","parent_question":5,"topic":"sub-programs (function with parameter and return)","marks":3,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"When a player completes a level, they move to the next level. Once level 3 is completed, the game starts again at level 1."},{"type":"text","value":"Write a function called nextlevel() that:\\n• takes the current level as a parameter\\n• works out the integer value of the next level the player moves to\\n• returns the integer value."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nfunction nextlevel(oldlevel)\\n  if oldlevel == 3 then\\n    return 1\\n  else\\n    return oldlevel + 1\\n  endif\\nend function\\nAccept correct use of MOD for BP2 and 3. Allow FT for BP3 if value output/calculated but not returned.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"function nextlevel() defined with at least one parameter","marks":1},{"criteria":"Returns parameter plus 1","marks":1},{"criteria":"...except for if parameter is 3, then returns 1","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"5(iii)","parent_question":5,"topic":"sub-programs (calling a function)","marks":1,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Complete the line of code to output the value returned from the function nextlevel() when the integer value 3 is passed in as a parameter."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"print(____(____))"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Allow other logically correct answers.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"print(nextlevel(3))","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"6(a)(i)","parent_question":6,"topic":"SQL SELECT/FROM/WHERE with AND","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"OCR Drones flies goods around the country using drones. Details about the drones that pilots fly are stored in a database table called TblDrone. Some of the data stored in this table is shown."},{"type":"table","headers":["DroneID","DroneType","Mileage","LastCheck"],"rows":[["001","Quadcopter","65 032","65 000"],["002","Quadcopter","32 128","21 000"],["003","Octocopter","98 021","98 000"]]},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the SQL statement to display DroneID and Mileage for all Octocopter type drones that have a mileage of greater than 50 000 miles."},{"type":"code","language":"sql","value":"SELECT ____\\n____ TblDrone\\nWHERE DroneType = \\"Octocopter\\" ____ Mileage ____"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Accept SELECT * or selection of additional fields for BP1.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"SELECT DroneID, Mileage","marks":1},{"criteria":"FROM","marks":1},{"criteria":"AND","marks":1},{"criteria":"> 50000","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"6(a)(ii)","parent_question":6,"topic":"flowchart (selection / comparison)","marks":2,"command_word":"complete","response_style":"annotate-image","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Drones must be checked every 10 000 miles. If the difference between Mileage and LastCheck is greater than 10 000 then the drone needs to be checked."},{"type":"text","value":"A flowchart shows the steps needed to check a drone. The flowchart outputs \\"Check\\" if the drone needs to be checked. The flowchart outputs \\"No Check\\" if the drone does not need to be checked."},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the flowchart for the algorithm."},{"type":"image","kind":"diagram","src":"j277/topics/ocr/2.2.3_q6aii_drone_flowchart_canvas.png","alt_text":"Drone-check flowchart with the comparison condition and output labels left empty for the candidate to complete."}],"answer":{"guidance":"BP1 could be >, < or either in words. Ignore case and minor misspellings. BP2 (output) could be either way around depending on comparison for BP1.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"if Mileage - LastCheck > 10000 (correct comparison)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Output \\"Check\\" and \\"No Check\\" (or equivalent) correctly based on logical check","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"6(b)","parent_question":6,"topic":"random number generation and trace tables","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A pilot code is automatically generated when a new pilot joins the company. This algorithm generates a code for each pilot:"},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"01 a = input(\\"Enter first letter of first name\\")\\n02 b = input(\\"Enter first letter of second name\\")\\n03 c = random(1,100)\\n04 while c < 100\\n05   c = c * 10\\n06 endwhile\\n07 pilotCode = a + b + str(c)\\n08 print(pilotCode)"},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the trace table for the given algorithm. Lines 01 to 03 have already been completed. You may not need to use all rows in the trace table."},{"type":"table","headers":["Line number","a","b","c","pilotCode","Output"],"rows":[["01","H","","","",""],["02","","K","","",""],["03","","","9","",""],["","","","","",""],["","","","","",""],["","","","","",""],["","","","","",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"Ignore additional lines that do not affect outcome. FT for missing or incorrect line numbers. FT for output based on incorrect tracing of loop. 1 mark per row.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"c = 90 on line 05","marks":1},{"criteria":"c = 900 on line 05","marks":1},{"criteria":"pilotCode = HK900 on line 07","marks":1},{"criteria":"HK900 output on line 08","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"6(c)(i)","parent_question":6,"topic":"selection and calculation","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Pilots are paid a set amount each day. Pilots also get an additional payment for each mile they have flown that day. These payments are shown in the table."},{"type":"table","headers":["Flying experience","Pay per day","Pay per mile"],"rows":[["Fewer than 2 years","£120.00","£0.45"],["2 years to 5 years inclusive","£150.00","£0.65"],["More than 5 years","£180.00","£0.85"]]},{"type":"text","value":"For example, a pilot with 3 years\' experience who flies 100 miles in one day will receive a total of £215.00 pay. This is calculated in the following way:\\n• £150.00 pay for the day\\n• £65.00 additional payment (£0.65 pay per mile x 100 miles)\\n• Add £150.00 and £65.00 together to get £215.00 total pay"},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the algorithm to:\\n• Calculate the total pay for the pilot for that day\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"experience = input(\\"Enter years of experience\\")\\nmiles = input(\\"Enter miles flown\\")\\ntotalPay = 0\\n____\\nprint(totalPay)"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nif exp < 2 then\\n  totalPay = 120 + (0.45 * miles)\\nelseif exp <= 5 then\\n  totalPay = 150 + (0.65 * miles)\\nelse\\n  totalPay = 180 + (0.85 * miles)\\nend if\\nFT for BP4 only where a reasonable attempt at calculating pay has been made.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Attempt at using selection","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates pay correctly for pilots with less than 2 years experience","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates pay correctly for pilots with 2 to 5 years experience (must include both 2 and 5)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates pay correctly for pilots with more than 5 years experience","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"6(c)(ii)","parent_question":6,"topic":"sub-programs (using a function)","marks":2,"command_word":"refine","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The programmer decides to make a function to calculate the total pay for the pilot. The function is called calculatePay(). The function takes the values for experience and miles as two parameters and returns the total pay for the pilot. Refine the algorithm to use this function and output the pay for the pilot."},{"type":"text","value":"You must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"experience = input(\\"Enter years of experience\\")\\nmiles = input(\\"Enter miles flown\\")\\n\\n____ = calculatePay( ____ , ____ )\\n\\nprint( totalPay )"}],"answer":{"guidance":"totalPay = calculatePay(experience, miles). Order of parameters acceptable either way (experience, miles) or (miles, experience).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"totalPay (as assignment target)","marks":1},{"criteria":"(experience, miles) // (miles, experience) as parameters","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"7(a)","parent_question":7,"topic":"sub-programs (procedures, selection with Boolean)","marks":4,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"An alarm has an algorithm that decides whether to sound the alarm by checking the data that is stored in the following three variables.\\n• SystemArmed\\n• DoorSensorActive\\n• WindowSensorActive"},{"type":"text","value":"The alarm will only sound when the alarm has been activated and one or both of the door and window sensors are activated. When the system needs to sound the alarm it calls the pre-written procedure SoundAlarm()."},{"type":"text","value":"Write a program that checks the data in the variables and calls SoundAlarm() when appropriate.\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nif SystemArmed then\\n  if DoorSensorActive then\\n    SoundAlarm()\\n  else if WindowSensorActive then\\n    SoundAlarm()\\n  endif\\nendif\\nSelection could be done using IF, case, or any other sensible valid method. Allow True/False as strings. Only award BP4 if SoundAlarm correctly called/not called in every situation. Watch for precedence errors (use brackets for (Door OR Window)).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Attempt at using selection / condition controlled loop","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checking if system armed // while system armed","marks":1},{"criteria":"If Door Sensor active OR Window Sensor active (both checks required)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calling SoundAlarm correctly","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"7(b)","parent_question":7,"topic":"SQL SELECT/FROM/WHERE with AND","marks":3,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"An alarm system has a log that stores a record each time a sensor is triggered. This is called an event. The record format is given in the table:"},{"type":"table","headers":["Fieldname","Description"],"rows":[["Date","The date the event happened"],["SensorID","The sensor that was activated"],["SensorType","The type of sensor that was activated – Door, Motion or Window"],["Length","The number of seconds the sensor was triggered (to the nearest second)"]]},{"type":"text","value":"The log is stored in a database table called events. The current contents of events is shown:"},{"type":"table","headers":["Date","SensorID","SensorType","Length"],"rows":[["05/02/2023","WS2","Window","38"],["05/02/2023","MS1","Motion","2"],["06/02/2023","DS3","Door","1"],["06/02/2023","MS2","Motion","3"],["06/02/2023","MS1","Motion","2"],["07/02/2023","WS1","Window","24"],["07/02/2023","DS1","Door","1"]]},{"type":"text","value":"Write an SQL statement to display the sensor IDs of the door sensors that have been triggered for more than 20 seconds."}],"answer":{"guidance":"SELECT SensorID\\nFROM events\\nWHERE Length > 20 AND SensorType = \\"Door\\"\\nMax 2 if out of order or anything extra that affects the output. BP1 can select multiple fields as long as SensorID is included. \\"door\\" must be in quotation marks for BP3. Allow alternative WHERE clauses that are logically correct (e.g. WHERE length >= 21).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"SELECT SensorID (or SELECT *)","marks":1},{"criteria":"FROM events","marks":1},{"criteria":"WHERE Length > 20 AND SensorType = \\"Door\\" (or equivalent)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"7(c)","parent_question":7,"topic":"sub-programs (procedures) and file handling (open/write/close)","marks":6,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A program written in a high-level language is used to access the data from a database. This program has a procedure, SaveLogs(), that stores the data to an external text file."},{"type":"text","value":"The procedure SaveLogs():\\n• takes the string of data to be stored to the text file as a parameter\\n• takes the filename of the text file as a parameter\\n• stores the string of data to the text file."},{"type":"text","value":"Write the procedure SaveLogs()\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nprocedure SaveLogs(data, filename)\\n  logFile = open(filename)\\n  logFile.writeLine(data)\\n  logFile.close()\\nendprocedure\\nMust be clear that answer is a procedure definition. Allow function definition. If parameters overwritten, do not credit BP2 but FT for BP4 and 6. If code given outside of procedure, do not give BP4 and BP6.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Define procedure SaveLogs","marks":1},{"criteria":"...with two valid parameters","marks":1},{"criteria":"Open file (for write/append)","marks":1},{"criteria":"...using the file name passed in as parameter","marks":1},{"criteria":"Write data to file using the data passed in as parameter","marks":1},{"criteria":"Close file","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"7(d)(i)","parent_question":7,"topic":"casting (integer to string)","marks":1,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"OCR Security Services need to identify the total number of seconds the sensors have been activated on a specific date. The data from the database table events is imported into the program written in a high-level programming language. The program stores the data in a two-dimensional (2D) string array with the identifier arrayEvents."},{"type":"text","value":"The data to be stored is shown in the table."},{"type":"table","headers":["Date","SensorID","SensorType","Length"],"rows":[["05/02/2023","WS2","Window","38"],["05/02/2023","MS1","Motion","2"],["06/02/2023","DS3","Door","1"],["06/02/2023","MS2","Motion","3"],["06/02/2023","MS1","Motion","2"],["07/02/2023","WS1","Window","24"],["07/02/2023","DS1","Door","1"]]},{"type":"text","value":"In this table, the value of events[1, 1] contains \\"MS1\\"."},{"type":"text","value":"An array can only store data of one data type. Any non-string data must be converted to a string before storing in the array."},{"type":"text","value":"Identify the process that converts integer data to string data."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Accept type casting. Do not accept conversion. Do not accept examples of casting.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Casting / cast (or type casting)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"7(d)(ii)","parent_question":7,"topic":"2D arrays, iteration, selection, running total","marks":6,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Write a program that:\\n• asks the user to input a date\\n• totals the number of seconds sensors have been activated on the date input\\n• outputs the calculated total in an appropriate message including the date, for example:"},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"Sensors were activated for 40 seconds on 05/02/2023"},{"type":"text","value":"You must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\ntotal = 0\\ndate = input(\\"Please enter date\\")\\nfor count = 0 to events.length-1\\n  if events[0, count] == date then\\n    total = total + events[3, count]\\n  endif\\nnext count\\nprint(\\"There were \\" + total + \\" events on \\" + date)\\nBP2 loop allow off by one errors, looping to array length or array length - 1. BP4/5 allow array reference as either column major or row major. Only give output mark if attempt made to calculate total within the algorithm. Must be 0 to 6, not 1 to 7.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Input date and store in variable / use directly","marks":1},{"criteria":"Access all seven (indexes 0 to 6) events in array // loop for each event in array","marks":1},{"criteria":"Attempt at selection","marks":1},{"criteria":"...to compare date input against date in array (element 0)","marks":1},{"criteria":"...adding length (element 3) from array to the total if dates match","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputting calculated total and date in appropriate message(s) at the end","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(a)(i)","parent_question":8,"topic":"data types (records)","marks":2,"command_word":"state","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Customers at a hotel can stay between 1 and 5 (inclusive) nights and can choose between a basic room or a premium room. A typical booking record is shown in the table:"},{"type":"table","headers":["Field","Value"],"rows":[["firstName","Amaya"],["surname","Taylor-Ling"],["nights","3"],["room","Premium"],["stayComplete","False"]]},{"type":"text","value":"State the most appropriate data type for the following fields:\\nNights\\nRoom"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Accept other valid data types from high-level languages (e.g. byte, short for integers). Do not accept descriptions (e.g. \\"whole number\\", \\"text\\"). Do not accept \\"character(s)\\" for string.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Nights: Integer","marks":1},{"criteria":"Room: String","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(a)(ii)","parent_question":8,"topic":"data types (Boolean)","marks":1,"command_word":"give","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Give the name of one field that could be stored as a Boolean data type."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Ignore spaces or misspelling as long as recognisable.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"stayComplete","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(a)(iii)","parent_question":8,"topic":"SQL SELECT/FROM/WHERE","marks":4,"command_word":"rewrite","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Booking records are stored in a database table called TblBookings. The following SQL statement is written to display all customer bookings that stay more than one night."},{"type":"code","language":"sql","value":"SELECT ALL\\nFROM TblBookings\\nIF Nights < 1"},{"type":"text","value":"The SQL statement is incorrect. Rewrite the SQL statement so that it is correct."}],"answer":{"guidance":"SELECT FirstName, Surname, Nights, Room, StayComplete // SELECT *\\nFROM TblBookings\\nWHERE Nights > 1 // Nights >= 2 // Nights BETWEEN 2 AND 5\\nOrder of fields for BP1 not important but must show all fields and be separated by commas. Spelling must be correct. Max 3 if in wrong order or if includes any extra invalid code.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"SELECT FirstName, Surname, Nights, Room, StayComplete (or SELECT *)","marks":1},{"criteria":"FROM TblBookings (unchanged, correct)","marks":1},{"criteria":"WHERE (replacing IF)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Nights > 1 (or Nights >= 2 / Nights BETWEEN 2 AND 5)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(b)(i)","parent_question":8,"topic":"input validation with Booleans","marks":5,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"When a new booking is recorded, the details are entered into a program to validate the values. The following criteria are checked:\\n• `firstName` and `surname` are not empty\\n• `room` is either \\"basic\\" or \\"premium\\"\\n• `nights` is between 1 and 5 (inclusive).\\nIf any invalid data is found \\"NOT ALLOWED\\" is displayed. If all data is valid \\"ALLOWED\\" is displayed."},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the following program to validate the inputs. You must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• a high-level programming language that you have studied."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"firstName = input(\\"Enter a first name\\")\\nsurname = input(\\"Enter a surname\\")\\nroom = input(\\"Enter basic or premium\\")\\nnights = input(\\"Enter between 1 and 5 nights\\")\\nstayComplete = False\\n# Complete the program below"}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"},{"type":"code","value":"valid = True\\nif firstname == \\"\\" or surname == \\"\\" then\\n  valid = False\\nendif\\nif room != \\"basic\\" and room != \\"premium\\" then\\n  valid = False\\nendif\\nif nights < 1 or nights > 5 then\\n  valid = False\\nendif\\nif valid then\\n  print(\\"ALLOWED\\")\\nelse\\n  print(\\"NOT ALLOWED\\")\\nendif"},{"type":"list","items":["Must have some attempt at all three checks to give output mark(s).","Check for nights must check both upper and lower limits.","Do not accept logically incorrect Boolean conditions such as `if firstname or surname == \\"\\"`."]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Checks that both firstname and surname are not empty","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks that room is either \\"basic\\" or \\"premium\\"","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks that nights is between 1 and 5 (inclusive)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputs \\"NOT ALLOWED\\" (or equivalent) if any of the 3 checks are invalid","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputs \\"ALLOWED\\" (or equivalent) only if all three checks are valid","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(b)(ii)","parent_question":8,"topic":"test data (normal, boundary, erroneous)","marks":3,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Complete the following test plan to check whether the number of nights is validated correctly."},{"type":"table","headers":["Test data (number of nights)","Type of test","Expected output"],"rows":[["2","","ALLOWED"],["","Boundary","ALLOWED"],["","Erroneous / Invalid","NOT ALLOWED"]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"Allow other descriptions that mean normal (e.g. valid / typical / acceptable).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Normal (for test data 2)","marks":1},{"criteria":"1 or 5 (boundary value; not 0 or 6 as says allowed)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Any numeric value except 1 to 5 // any non-numeric input (e.g. 7 or \\"bananas\\")","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(c)(i)","parent_question":8,"topic":"sub-programs (function with multiple parameters)","marks":4,"command_word":"create","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A Basic room costs £60 each night. A Premium room costs £80 each night."},{"type":"text","value":"Create a function, newPrice(), that takes the number of nights and the type of room as parameters, calculates and returns the price to pay. You do not have to validate these parameters."},{"type":"text","value":"You must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• a high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nfunction newPrice(nights, room)\\n  if room == \\"basic\\" then\\n    price = 60 * nights\\n  elseif room == \\"premium\\" then\\n    price = 80 * nights\\n  endif\\n  return price\\nendfunction\\nBP1 must be clear that a new function is being defined. Allow FT for subsequent marks if not present. If inputs used instead of parameters, FT for BP3. Must return (not output) value.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Function header for newPrice","marks":1},{"criteria":"...taking (at least) two parameters","marks":1},{"criteria":"...correctly calculates price based on parameters within function","marks":1},{"criteria":"...returns this calculated price","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(c)(ii)","parent_question":8,"topic":"sub-programs (calling a function)","marks":3,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Write program code, that uses newPrice(), to output the price of staying in a Premium room for 5 nights."},{"type":"text","value":"You must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• a high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"e.g. print(newPrice(\\"premium\\", 5)) or x = newPrice(5, \\"premium\\"); print(x). Order of parameters not important. \\"premium\\" must use string delimiters. Do not allow function definitions for BP1.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Call function newPrice","marks":1},{"criteria":"...with (\\"premium\\", 5) as parameters","marks":1},{"criteria":"Output returned value","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(d)","parent_question":8,"topic":"iteration, selection, input/output","marks":6,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A hotel car park charges £4 per hour. If the car is electric, this price is halved to £2 per hour."},{"type":"text","value":"Write an algorithm to:\\n• take as input the number of hours the user has parked and whether their car is electric or not\\n• calculate and output the total price\\n• repeat continually until the user enters 0 hours.\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• a high level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nwhile hours != 0\\n  hours = input(\\"Enter hours\\")\\n  electric = input(\\"enter Y for electric or N\\")\\n  if electric == \\"Y\\" then\\n    price = hours * 2\\n  elseif electric == \\"N\\" then\\n    price = hours * 4\\n  endif\\n  print(price)\\nendwhile\\nInitialisation of price and hours not necessary. BP5 must include all points attempted. BP6 can be given as FT even if BP5 (loop) is in the wrong place.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Inputs hours AND electric (two separate inputs), storing or using these","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks if car is electric (IF/Select statement)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Correctly calculates and outputs price (hours * 2 // price / 2) for electric","marks":1},{"criteria":"Correctly calculates and outputs price (hours * 4 // electric price * 2) for non-electric","marks":1},{"criteria":"Attempt at repetition of BP1 to 4","marks":1},{"criteria":"...until 0 hours entered","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"9","parent_question":9,"topic":"SQL SELECT/FROM/WHERE","marks":3,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The database table Results stores the results for each student in each of their chosen subjects."},{"type":"table","headers":["StudentName","Subject","Grade"],"rows":[["Alistair","English","3"],["Jaxon","Art","5"],["Alex","Art","4"],["Anna","French","7"],["Ismaael","Art","9"]]},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the SQL query to return all of the fields for the students who take Art."},{"type":"code","language":"sql","value":"SELECT ____\\nFROM ____\\nWHERE ____"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Correct Answer Only. Accept SELECT *.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"SELECT StudentName, Subject, Grade (or SELECT *)","marks":1},{"criteria":"FROM Results","marks":1},{"criteria":"WHERE Subject = \\"Art\\"","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"10","parent_question":10,"topic":"sub-programs (calling a function and storing return value)","marks":2,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A cinema uses the following criteria to decide if a customer is allowed to see a film that has a 15 rating: Customers have to be 15 years of age or older to see the film. They also need to either have a ticket or have the money to buy a ticket."},{"type":"text","value":"The table shows the inputs to the system that will output whether the customer can watch the film."},{"type":"table","headers":["Input","Criteria (True / False)"],"rows":[["A","The customer is 15 or over"],["B","The customer has a ticket"],["C","The customer has the money to buy a ticket"]]},{"type":"text","value":"The cinema has three screens: \\"Red\\", \\"Black\\" and \\"Yellow\\". The function freeseats() counts how many seats are available in each screen. The name of the screen is passed in as a string parameter and the number of free seats is returned as an integer."},{"type":"text","value":"Write code using the function freeseats() to find the number of seats available in screen Red and assign this to a variable with identifier redseats."}],"answer":{"guidance":"redseats = freeseats(\\"Red\\"). \\"Red\\" must use suitable string delimiters (e.g. speech marks) if directly passing the string. Do not penalise case.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"freeseats called with \\"Red\\"","marks":1},{"criteria":"...returned value assigned to variable redseats","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"11(a)","parent_question":11,"topic":"SQL SELECT/FROM/WHERE (multiple choice)","marks":3,"command_word":"tick","content":[{"type":"text","value":"OCR Tech is an online shop that sells electronics such as TVs and game consoles."},{"type":"text","value":"Items for sale are stored in the database table `tblStock`. An extract of this table is shown."},{"type":"table","headers":["ItemCode","ItemName","Price (£)","Stock"],"rows":[["GSC5","GameStation5 console","249.99","102"],["TV4K","4K Television","499.99","18"],["ABRR","Audiobook reader","59.99","27"],["NAGC","TV streaming stick","24.99","192"]]},{"type":"text","value":"Tick one box in each section to identify the correct SQL statement to select the item code and item name for all items that have a price of £60 or over."},{"type":"table","headers":["SELECT clause","Tick one box"],"rows":[["SELECT ItemCode AND ItemName",""],["SELECT ItemCode, ItemName",""],["SELECT ItemCode & ItemName",""]]},{"type":"table","headers":["FROM clause","Tick one box"],"rows":[["FROM tblStock",""],["FROM table",""],["FROM database",""]]},{"type":"table","headers":["WHERE clause","Tick one box"],"rows":[["WHERE Price <= 60",""],["WHERE Price > 60",""],["WHERE Price >= 60",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"One mark per correct choice. Accept other markings that indicate a choice has been made (e.g. a cross, etc).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"SELECT ItemCode, ItemName","marks":1},{"criteria":"FROM tblStock","marks":1},{"criteria":"WHERE Price >= 60","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"11(b)(i)","parent_question":11,"topic":"2D arrays and sub-programs (function with iteration)","marks":5,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Customers can use a discount code to reduce the price of their purchase. Valid discount codes and their value (in pounds) are stored in a global two-dimensional (2D) array with the identifier `discount`. The following table shows part of this 2D array."},{"type":"table","headers":["Index","Column [0]","Column [1]"],"rows":[["[0]","PVFC7","10"],["[1]","CPU5","5"],["[2]","BGF2","15"]],"caption":"discount"},{"type":"text","value":"For example, `discount[2,0]` holds discount code BGF2 and `discount[2,1]` holds the discount of 15 pounds."},{"type":"text","value":"A function searches through the 2D array and applies the discount to the price. The price and discount code are passed in as parameters. The algorithm design is not complete."},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the design for the algorithm."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"function checkdiscount(price, code)\\n  newprice = price\\n  size = len(discount) – 1\\n  for x = 0 to ____\\n    if discount[x,0] == ____ then\\n      newprice = ____ – discount[____]\\n    endif\\n  next x\\n  ____\\nendfunction"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nfunction checkdiscount(price, code)\\n  newprice = price\\n  size = len(discount)-1\\n  for x = 0 to size\\n    if discount[x,0] == code then\\n      newprice = price – discount[x,1]\\n    endif\\n  next\\n  return newprice\\nendfunction\\nOne mark per bullet point, in the correct place.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Upper bound: size // len(discountcodes)-1","marks":1},{"criteria":"Comparison value: code","marks":1},{"criteria":"Subtraction base: price // newprice","marks":1},{"criteria":"Discount index: [x,1] // [x][1]","marks":1},{"criteria":"return newprice // checkdiscount = newprice","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"11(b)(ii)","parent_question":11,"topic":"variables (identifying)","marks":2,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The function design from part (i) is shown below."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"function checkdiscount(price, code)\\n  newprice = price\\n  size = len(discount) - 1\\n  for x = 0 to [missing value]\\n    if discount[x,0] == [missing value] then\\n      newprice = [missing value] - discount[[missing value]]\\n    endif\\n  next x\\n  [missing statement]\\nendfunction"},{"type":"text","value":"Identify two variables used in this function design."},{"type":"text","value":"1: ____"},{"type":"text","value":"2: ____"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Do not penalise capitalisation. Accept price, code, discount.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Any one of: newprice / size / x (or price / code / discount)","marks":1},{"criteria":"A second one of: newprice / size / x (or price / code / discount)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"11(b)(iii)","parent_question":11,"topic":"sub-programs (using a function), iteration, running total","marks":6,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Write a program that:\\n• asks the user for an item price and discount code\\n• uses the checkdiscount() function from part (i) to calculate the price of the item after any discount has been applied\\n• repeats bullet points 1 and 2 until a price of 0 is entered\\n• outputs the total cost of all items entered, after any discounts have been applied."},{"type":"text","value":"You must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\ntotal = 0\\ndo\\n  price = input(\\"Enter a price\\")\\n  code = input(\\"Enter a discount code\\")\\n  newprice = checkdiscount(price, code)\\n  total = total + newprice\\nuntil price == 0\\nprint(total)\\nHigh-level programming language / OCR Exam Reference Language response required. Do not accept pseudocode / natural language. BP3 allow total of prices entered as FT if candidate does not achieve BP2.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Asks for price and discount code to be input","marks":1},{"criteria":"...passes both to the checkdiscount() function as parameters","marks":1},{"criteria":"...stores / uses returned value","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates total of all prices entered/returned","marks":1},{"criteria":"Repeats until 0 is entered as price","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputs calculated total","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"12","parent_question":12,"topic":"2D arrays (accessing element)","marks":1,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Data for one week (Monday to Friday) is stored in a 2D array with the identifier `minsPlayed`. The following table shows part of this array, containing 4 students."},{"type":"table","headers":["Day","Row index","Stuart (col 0)","Wes (col 1)","Victoria (col 2)","Dan (col 3)"],"rows":[["Mon","0","60","30","45","0"],["Tue","1","180","60","0","60"],["Wed","2","200","30","0","20"],["Thu","3","60","10","15","15"],["Fri","4","100","35","30","45"]],"caption":"minsPlayed (rows = days of the week, columns = students)"},{"type":"text","value":"The teacher wants to output the number of minutes Dan (column index 3) played computer games on Wednesday (row index 2). The following code is written:"},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"print(minsPlayed[3,2])"},{"type":"text","value":"Write program code to output the number of minutes that Stuart played computer games on Friday. You must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• a high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"High-level programming language / OCR Exam Reference Language response required. Do not accept pseudocode / natural English. The array elements may be accessed together [0,4] (VB.NET) or separately [0][4] (Python).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"print(minsPlayed[0,4]) (or equivalent access of the correct element)","marks":1}]}}]'),dE={paper_id:aE,qualification:rE,component:nE,title:iE,year:sE,session:oE,total_marks:cE,questions:lE},uE="J277-TOPIC-2.3.2",pE="J277",hE="TOPIC",mE="Testing",fE=null,gE=null,_E=109,yE=JSON.parse('[{"question_id":"1","parent_question":1,"topic":"test data