iteria":"Any normal value (between 40 and 180 inclusive)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Boundary: 40.0 // 180.0","marks":1},{"criteria":"Erroneous: any value less than 40 // any value greater than 180 // any non-numeric value","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(d)","parent_question":2,"topic":"SQL","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The individual results for each student in each event are stored in a database. The database table TblResult stores the times of students in the 100 m race. Some of the data is shown:"},{"type":"table","headers":["StudentID","YearGroup","TeamName","Time"],"rows":[["11GC1","11","Valiants",""],["10VE1","10","Super-Team","20.3"],["10SM1","10","Super-Team","19.7"],["11JP2","11","Champions","19.2"],["","","","19.65"]]},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the SQL statement to show the Student ID and team name of all students who are in year group 11."},{"type":"code","language":"sql","value":"SELECT StudentID, ____\\nFROM ____\\n____"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Max 3 if not in correct order / includes other logical errors. Ignore capitals. Do not accept * or additional fields for BP1. Spelling must be accurate (e.g. not TblResults). No spaces in field names, penalise obvious spaces once and then FT. Allow quotation marks around field names, table name and 11. Accept == for BP4 (invalid SQL but works in some environments).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"TeamName only in first space","marks":1},{"criteria":"TblResult in second space","marks":1},{"criteria":"WHERE","marks":1},{"criteria":"YearGroup = 11","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(e)(i)","parent_question":2,"topic":"abstraction","marks":1,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Abstraction and decomposition have been used in the design of the sports day program."},{"type":"text","value":"Identify one way that abstraction has been used in the design of this program."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Must be applicable to this program (in the context of stude