anguage that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example 1:\\nhighscore = 0\\nwhile team != \\"stop\\"\\n  team = input(\\"enter team name\\")\\n  score = input(\\"enter score\\")\\n  if score > highscore then\\n    highscore = score\\n    highteam = team\\n  endif\\nendwhile\\nprint(highscore)\\nprint(highteam)\\n\\nFor BP3, allow \\"stop\\" to be entered for either team name or score (or both). Allow use of break (or equivalent) to exit loop for BP3. Allow use of recursive function(s) for BP2/3. Initialisation of variables not needed. Ignore that multiple teams could get the same high score. BP4/5 could be done in many ways. Allow any logically valid method. Allow use of max/sum functions and use of arrays/lists. FT for BP6 if attempt made at calculating highest score/name. If answer simply asks for multiple entries (not using iteration), BP2 and 3 cannot be accessed but all others available. input cannot be used as a variable name.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Input team name AND score and store / use separately","marks":1},{"criteria":"Attempt at using iteration","marks":1},{"criteria":"To enter team/score until \\"stop\\" entered","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates highest score","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates winning team name","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputs highest score and team name","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"3(a)","parent_question":3,"topic":"types of errors (syntax)","marks":2,"command_word":"state","content":[{"type":"text","value":"State what is meant by the term syntax error. Give one example of a syntax error in a program."},{"type":"text","value":"Give your answer in the form:\\nDefinition: <state what is meant by a syntax error>\\nExample: <give one example of a syntax error in a program>"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Max 1 mark for definition that is clearly different from a logic error. BOD code/program etc for definition. Do not allow answers linked to data types. \\"incorrect grammar\\" by itself is NE. Do not allow \\"stop workin