ks":1},{"criteria":"Kofi2021x as staffID on line 05","marks":1},{"criteria":"Kofi2021xx as staffID on line 05","marks":1},{"criteria":"ID Kofi2021xx output on line 07 as first and only output","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"9(i)","parent_question":9,"topic":"validation algorithm","marks":5,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Customers at a hotel can stay between 1 and 5 (inclusive) nights and can choose between a basic room or a premium room."},{"type":"text","value":"When a new booking is recorded, the details are entered into a program to validate the values. The following criteria are checked:\\n- `firstName` and `surname` are not empty\\n- `room` is either \\"basic\\" or \\"premium\\"\\n- `nights` is between 1 and 5 (inclusive).\\nIf any invalid data is found \\"NOT ALLOWED\\" is displayed.\\nIf all data is valid \\"ALLOWED\\" is displayed."},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the following program to validate the inputs."},{"type":"text","value":"You must use either:\\n- OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n- a high-level programming language that you have studied."},{"type":"code","language":"pseudocode","value":"firstName = input(\\"Enter a first name\\")\\n\\nsurname = input(\\"Enter a surname\\")\\n\\nroom = input(\\"Enter basic or premium\\")\\n\\nnights = input(\\"Enter between 1 and 5 nights\\")\\n\\nstayComplete = False"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Must have some attempt at all three checks to give output mark(s). Check for nights must check both upper and lower limits. Iteration can be used as validation if input repeatedly asked for until valid answer given. Do not accept logically incorrect Boolean conditions such as if firstname or surname == \\"\\". Do not accept descriptive symbols for >=, <=. Ignore capitalisation. Example:\\nvalid = True\\nif firstname == \\"\\" or surname == \\"\\" then\\n  valid = False\\nendif\\nif room != \\"basic\\" and room != \\"premium\\" then\\n  valid = False\\nendif\\nif nights < 1 or nights > 5 then\\n  valid = False\\nendif\\nif valid then\\n  print(\\"ALLOWED\\")\\nelse\\n  print(\\"NOT ALLOWED\\")\\nendif\\nBP1 to 3 can check for valid or invalid inputs. Pay particular attention to use of AND / OR. Only give marks for output if these work together correctly.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Checks that both firstname and surname are not empty","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks that room is either \\"basic\\" or \\"premium\\"","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks that nights is between 1 and 5 (inclusive)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputs \\"NOT ALLOWED\\" (or equivalent) if any of the 3 checks are invalid (must check all three)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputs \\"ALLOWED\\" (or equivalent) only if all three checks are valid (must check all three)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"9(ii)","parent_question":9,"topic":"test plan (normal, boundary, erroneous)","marks":3,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Complete the following test plan to check whether the number of nights is validated correctly."},{"type":"table","headers":["Test data (number of nights)","Type of test","Expected output"],"rows":[["2","","ALLOWED"],["","Boundary","ALLOWED"],["","Erroneous / Invalid","NOT ALLOWED"]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"Allow other descriptions that mean normal (e.g. valid / typical / acceptable).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"First row: Normal","marks":1},{"criteria":"Boundary row test data: 1 or 5 (not 0 or 6 as says allowed)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Erroneous row test data: Any numeric value except 1 to 5 // any non-numeric input (e.g. \\"bananas\\")","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"10(i)","parent_question":10,"topic":"validation algorithm","marks":5,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A car dealership uses a computer system to record details of the cars that it has for sale. Each car has a make, model, age and number of miles driven."},{"type":"text","value":"The car dealership only sells cars that have fewer than 10 000 miles and are 5 years old or less."},{"type":"text","value":"Write an algorithm that will:\\n- ask the user to enter the number of miles and the age of a car\\n- validate the input to check that only sensible values that are in the given range are entered\\n- output True if valid data has been entered or False if invalid data has been entered."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark per bullet, max 4 for BP1-4; BP5 for outputs. BP2 and 3 must check for both ends of range - must check that input data is not negative. Allow FT for BP4 if already penalised under BP2 and/or 3 and output is otherwise correct. Example:\\nmiles = input(\\"enter miles driven\\")\\nage = input(\\"enter age of car\\")\\nvalid = True\\nif miles > 10000 or miles < 0 then\\n  valid = False\\nelseif age > 5 or age < 0 then\\n  valid = False\\nendif\\nprint(valid)","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Miles and age input separately","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks for valid mileage","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks for valid age","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks both are greater than / greater than equal to zero","marks":1},{"criteria":"Correctly outputs both True and False","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"10(ii)","parent_question":10,"topic":"test data (normal, erroneous, boundary)","marks":3,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The validation routine from part (i) must be tested with normal, erroneous and boundary test data. Identify suitable test data for each type of test."},{"type":"table","headers":["","Miles","Age"],"rows":[["Normal","",""],["Erroneous","",""],["Boundary","",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark per row, max 3. Specific data must be given, not a description. e.g. Normal: 7,000 and 3; Erroneous: 12,000 and 7; Boundary: 10,000 and 5.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Normal: miles (0-9,999), age (0-5)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Erroneous: miles (less than 0, larger than 9,999), age (less than 0 / more than 5) // non-numeric data","marks":1},{"criteria":"Boundary: miles (-1/0/9,999/10,000), age 